                <pb facs="0742" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.811/8–2048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Erhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-20">August 20,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1017. Council of Ministers issued statement yesterday that Austria is not bound
                    by Danube agreement concluded by eastern countries; and that as soon Austria can
                    take part as member with full rights in negotiations concerned with this
                    question it will undertake examination of merits of this agreement.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept; repeated Belgrade as 337.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Erhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
